          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पूर्वजः (pūrvajaḥ) is built from pūrva, \"earlier, former\", and ja, \"born\", from the root √jan; MW gives pūrvaja as born before, and an ancestor or forefather (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
